# Three Resolutions, Always

Every page and every component must be built for all three ranges at once. Resizing the browser
window must show blocks reflowing, never breaking or overflowing horizontally.

| Range   | Width          |
|---------|----------------|
| Mobile  | below 768px    |
| Tablet  | 768px–1023px   |
| Desktop | 1024px and up  |

## Mobile-first CSS

Write base styles for mobile, then layer the two breakpoints. Use only these two queries so the
breakpoints stay consistent across the codebase:

```css
.c-grid { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 1fr; gap: var(--sp-4); }

@media (min-width: 768px) {
  .c-grid { grid-template-columns: repeat(2, 1fr); }
}

@media (min-width: 1024px) {
  .c-grid { grid-template-columns: repeat(4, 1fr); }
}
```

## Rules

- No fixed pixel widths on layout containers. Use `%`, `fr`, `minmax()`, or `max-width`.
- Horizontal scroll on the page body is a bug. Long tables and card rows scroll inside their own
  container with a visible scroll affordance.
- Never hide content at a breakpoint to "fix" a layout. Reflow it instead.
- A section is not done until it has been checked at roughly 375px, 834px, and 1440px.
